## Exhaustiveness checking for multi-field nominal variants

# Define a type with multi-field nominal variants
AstNode: [type
  [IntLit value: Int span: Int]
  [StrLit value: String span: Int]
]

## Test 1: Exhaustive match on both variants (should pass, no warnings)
test-exhaustive: [fn [node@AstNode]:
  [match node
    [IntLit value: v span: s]: [+ v s]
    [StrLit value: v span: s]: [len v]
  ]
]

## Test 2: Non-exhaustive match (only one variant, should warn)
test-non-exhaustive: [fn [node@AstNode]:
  [match node
    [IntLit value: v span: s]: [+ v s]
  ]
]

=== warn
test-non-exhaustive: non-exhaustive match: missing cases:
  [StrLit value: _ span: _]
===

# Test that the types are correctly inferred
result1: [test-exhaustive [IntLit value: 42 span: 10]]
---
52
---

result2: [test-exhaustive [StrLit value: "hello" span: 5]]
---
5
---

# Non-exhaustive match should still evaluate correctly for covered cases
result3: [test-non-exhaustive [IntLit value: 100 span: 20]]
---
120
---
